LOCAL1="A window is shown flat"
LOCAL2="%s asked for two pictures of its window, one for each eye, and the Vulkan driver %s gives a window one picture only, so the window is shown flat. Programs that ask for 3D are shown flat on this driver until it gives two. Mesa's Vulkan drivers give two; for other drivers the package mesa-vulkan-layer-stereo gives them: check that it is installed and that DISABLE_LAYER_MESA_STEREO is not set."
LOCAL3="%s asked for two pictures of its window, one for each eye, and the OpenGL driver %s gives a window one picture only, so the window is shown flat. Programs that ask for 3D are shown flat on this driver until it gives two. Mesa's OpenGL gives two, also on an NVIDIA card through zink, as the desktop session sets it; a program started on NVIDIA's own OpenGL gets them from the gl-stereo layer."
LOCAL4="%s asked for two pictures of its window, one for each eye, and OpenGL runs on zink through its own swapchain, which shows one picture, so the window is shown flat. The desktop session sets LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE=1 with zink; start the program with it too."
LOCAL5="%s asked for two pictures of its window, one for each eye, and got them, but Qt draws its own frame around this window, and with the OpenGL driver %s it cannot draw that frame into both pictures, so the window is shown flat. The window shows its 3D when the desktop draws the window frames: choose a window decoration in System Settings."
